<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Salvage privacy manifest. It ships at Salvage.app/Contents/Resources/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy and
  covers everything inside the app bundle, including the embedded SalvageHelper (a bare executable
  in Contents/MacOS with no bundle of its own) and the SalvageCore / SalvageDiskIO packages, which
  are linked statically.

  No tracking, no tracking domains, no collected data: Salvage has no analytics, no account and no
  network code apart from the manual update check (docs/PRIVACY.md, scripts/check-no-network.sh).

  Required-reason APIs actually used (keep in sync with the code; re-grep before each release):

  - File timestamp APIs (stat / fstat / lstat):
      Salvage/ViewModels/RecoveryCoordinator.swift (fstat of files it writes into the folder the
      user chose), SalvageDiskIO ImageFileReader / DiskImageSource / ImageFileDestinationSafety
      (stat/fstat of a disk image the user picked), RawBlockReader and HelperShared (fstat/lstat of
      the device node the user picked, to confirm it is the expected character device).
      Only st_dev / st_ino / st_rdev / st_mode / st_size are read, never timestamps, but the API is listed.
      3B52.1: files and directories the user specifically granted access to.
  - System boot time (kern.boottime, mach_absolute_time via DispatchTime):
      Salvage/ViewModels/ScanArchive.swift (was a saved scan made in this boot?) and
      SalvageHelper/main.swift (idle-exit timer).
      35F9.1: measuring time elapsed between events within the app.
  - Disk space (volumeAvailableCapacity*Key, statfs / fstatfs / getfsstat):
      RecoveryCoordinator (free space on the recovery destination, shown to the user as a shortfall
      warning before recovering) and SalvageDiskIO DestinationSafety / BootDiskSafety /
      PrivilegedDiskQueries (which device a volume lives on).
      E174.1: checking there is enough space before writing files.
      85F4.1: showing disk-space information to the user.

  Not used, so not declared: UserDefaults / @AppStorage, active keyboard APIs.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>3B52.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>35F9.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>E174.1</string>
				<string>85F4.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
